/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The "Naija Way" is not just a catchy title; it is a philosophy. It acknowledges that while the principles of business are universal, their application is not. A business textbook from Harvard will teach you about SWOT analysis and Porter's Five Forces, but it won't teach you how to negotiate with a Lagos local government agent, how to maintain your brand's integrity when your customers demand "long leg," or how to build a loyal team in a culture where "pull him down" can be a silent mantra. The Naija Way is about applying timeless business wisdom through the lens of our unique reality our vibrant culture, our challenging infrastructure, our complex systems, and our unparalleled human spirit.)
/E (The "Naija Way" is not just a catchy title; it is a philosophy. It acknowledges that while the principles of business are universal, their application is not. A business textbook from Harvard will teach you about SWOT analysis and Porter's Five Forces, but it won't teach you how to negotiate with a Lagos local government agent, how to maintain your brand's integrity when your customers demand "long leg," or how to build a loyal team in a culture where "pull him down" can be a silent mantra. The Naija Way is about applying timeless business wisdom through the lens of our unique reality our vibrant culture, our challenging infrastructure, our complex systems, and our unparalleled human spirit.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
1123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (This playbook is not filled with theoretical fluff. It is a practical, step-by-step manual, a co-pilot on your journey. It is for the graduate with a degree but no practical roadmap, and for the non-graduate with a brilliant idea but no formal training. It is for the side-hustler ready to go full-time and the existing business owner feeling stuck.)
/E (This playbook is not filled with theoretical fluff. It is a practical, step-by-step manual, a co-pilot on your journey. It is for the graduate with a degree but no practical roadmap, and for the non-graduate with a brilliant idea but no formal training. It is for the side-hustler ready to go full-time and the existing business owner feeling stuck.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
