<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The Problem-Solution Matrix: Where Naija Gold is Hidden Global business theory often speaks of "identifying a gap in the market." In Nigeria, the "gaps" are less like discreet gaps and more like yawning chasms of unmet needs and inefficiencies. Our daily lives are a constant negotiation with challenges from the trivial to the profound. The successful Naija entrepreneur reframes these challenges not as burdens, but as a catalog of business opportunities.)
/E (The Problem-Solution Matrix: Where Naija Gold is Hidden Global business theory often speaks of "identifying a gap in the market." In Nigeria, the "gaps" are less like discreet gaps and more like yawning chasms of unmet needs and inefficiencies. Our daily lives are a constant negotiation with challenges from the trivial to the profound. The successful Naija entrepreneur reframes these challenges not as burdens, but as a catalog of business opportunities.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
