/T (The Nigerian business landscape is littered with the ghosts of "sure bets" that failed spectacularly. The restaurant with the secret family recipe that saw only three customers a day. The boutique selling beautiful Ankara styles that gathered dust on the racks. The tech solution that nobody downloaded. If you listen closely, you can almost hear the entrepreneurs' lament: "But I thought people would love it!")
