1195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (In Nigeria, "I think" is a dangerous foundation upon which to build your dreams and your capital. What separates the successful entrepreneur from the hopeful dreamer is the brutal, unglamorous discipline of turning assumptions into evidence. This chapter is about killing the "I think" mentality and replacing it with the most powerful phrase in business: "I know." Market research, in the Naija context, is not about expensive surveys or focus groups in air-conditioned halls. It is the art of gathering intelligence from the streets, from the markets, and from the very people you hope to serve. It is about listening not just to what people say, but to what they do.)
/E (In Nigeria, "I think" is a dangerous foundation upon which to build your dreams and your capital. What separates the successful entrepreneur from the hopeful dreamer is the brutal, unglamorous discipline of turning assumptions into evidence. This chapter is about killing the "I think" mentality and replacing it with the most powerful phrase in business: "I know." Market research, in the Naija context, is not about expensive surveys or focus groups in air-conditioned halls. It is the art of gathering intelligence from the streets, from the markets, and from the very people you hope to serve. It is about listening not just to what people say, but to what they do.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
