/T (The Trust Signal: In a market with a high trust deficit, a physical address is a powerful validator. For businesses selling high-value items \(e.g., electronics, jewellery\), perishable goods \(e.g., fresh groceries\), or products that require sensory inspection \(e.g., furniture, fabrics\), a store is almost non-negotiable. Customers can verify quality firsthand, reducing the perceived risk of purchase.)
/E (The Trust Signal: In a market with a high trust deficit, a physical address is a powerful validator. For businesses selling high-value items \(e.g., electronics, jewellery\), perishable goods \(e.g., fresh groceries\), or products that require sensory inspection \(e.g., furniture, fabrics\), a store is almost non-negotiable. Customers can verify quality firsthand, reducing the perceived risk of purchase.)
/Pg 64 0 R
/K [1]
