2178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Case Study: "Chinedu's Constructions": A Family Feud  Chinedu started a small building supplies store. As business boomed, he hired his younger brother, Emeka, as his store manager. Emeka was reliable but had a lax attitude towards record-keeping. Chinedu noticed inventory discrepancies but couldn't bring himself to confront Emeka directly. He dropped hints, which Emeka ignored. The problem grew until a major stock-taking revealed a significant loss. When Chinedu finally sat Emeka down for a formal meeting, Emeka was furious. "After all I've done for you? You are accusing me of theft? Is this how you treat your own blood?" The business meeting turned into a family shouting match. Emeka quit, and the brothers did not speak for two years. The business recovered, but the family fracture took much longer to heal.)
/E (Case Study: "Chinedu's Constructions": A Family Feud  Chinedu started a small building supplies store. As business boomed, he hired his younger brother, Emeka, as his store manager. Emeka was reliable but had a lax attitude towards record-keeping. Chinedu noticed inventory discrepancies but couldn't bring himself to confront Emeka directly. He dropped hints, which Emeka ignored. The problem grew until a major stock-taking revealed a significant loss. When Chinedu finally sat Emeka down for a formal meeting, Emeka was furious. "After all I've done for you? You are accusing me of theft? Is this how you treat your own blood?" The business meeting turned into a family shouting match. Emeka quit, and the brothers did not speak for two years. The business recovered, but the family fracture took much longer to heal.)
/Pg 93 0 R
/K [2]
