/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (For many Naija entrepreneurs, the world of numbers, ledgers, and financial statements is a mysterious and intimidating realm. It is often relegated to the "black box" a chaotic mix of mental calculations, scattered paper receipts, and a prayerful hope that the money in the business account is enough to cover the next expense. This approach is not just unprofessional; it is a direct threat to the very survival of your enterprise. A business without clear financial records is like a ship captain navigating a stormy ocean without a compass or a map. You might have a general sense of direction, but you have no real idea of your position, your speed, or the hidden rocks beneath the surface.)
/E (For many Naija entrepreneurs, the world of numbers, ledgers, and financial statements is a mysterious and intimidating realm. It is often relegated to the "black box" a chaotic mix of mental calculations, scattered paper receipts, and a prayerful hope that the money in the business account is enough to cover the next expense. This approach is not just unprofessional; it is a direct threat to the very survival of your enterprise. A business without clear financial records is like a ship captain navigating a stormy ocean without a compass or a map. You might have a general sense of direction, but you have no real idea of your position, your speed, or the hidden rocks beneath the surface.)
/Pg 101 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
