/P 6271 0 R
/T (Profit Illusion: The "Cash in Hand" Deception. This is the most common and fatal mistake. You see money flowing into your business account or your POS, you pay your major bills, and you assume the remainder is your profit. You then use this "profit" to cover personal expenses, only to find yourself stranded when a major tax bill, a bulk inventory purchase, or a equipment repair arises. Without proper records, you cannot distinguish between revenue, profit, and cash flow. You are essentially flying blind, celebrating what you think is success while heading for a crash.)
/E (Profit Illusion: The "Cash in Hand" Deception. This is the most common and fatal mistake. You see money flowing into your business account or your POS, you pay your major bills, and you assume the remainder is your profit. You then use this "profit" to cover personal expenses, only to find yourself stranded when a major tax bill, a bulk inventory purchase, or a equipment repair arises. Without proper records, you cannot distinguish between revenue, profit, and cash flow. You are essentially flying blind, celebrating what you think is success while heading for a crash.)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
2284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 6272 0 R
/T (The Tax Season Nightmare. When the tax authorities from FIRS or LIRS come knocking, they will demand to see your financial records. Showing up with a "black box" a bag of crumpled receipts and a confused story is an open invitation for trouble. They will use their own discretion to assess your tax liability, which will almost certainly be inflated, and you will have no records to contest it. Proper records are your shield and your evidence.)
/E (The Tax Season Nightmare. When the tax authorities from FIRS or LIRS come knocking, they will demand to see your financial records. Showing up with a "black box" a bag of crumpled receipts and a confused story is an open invitation for trouble. They will use their own discretion to assess your tax liability, which will almost certainly be inflated, and you will have no records to contest it. Proper records are your shield and your evidence.)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
