2293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (After two years, she decided to expand and applied for a loan. The bank asked for her financial statements. She had none. She hired an accountant who, over a painful month, pieced together her records from two years of bank statements, old receipts, and her memory. The conclusion was devastating. Bola had not made a profit in 18 months. The "profit" she had been spending was actually her working capital the money she needed to buy new stock. She was effectively consuming her own business to fund her lifestyle. The expansion dream was dead, and she had to drastically scale back her operations and personal spending to survive. This painful lesson could have been avoided with simple, consistent record-keeping.)
/E (After two years, she decided to expand and applied for a loan. The bank asked for her financial statements. She had none. She hired an accountant who, over a painful month, pieced together her records from two years of bank statements, old receipts, and her memory. The conclusion was devastating. Bola had not made a profit in 18 months. The "profit" she had been spending was actually her working capital the money she needed to buy new stock. She was effectively consuming her own business to fund her lifestyle. The expansion dream was dead, and she had to drastically scale back her operations and personal spending to survive. This painful lesson could have been avoided with simple, consistent record-keeping.)
/Pg 103 0 R
/K [0]
