/T (The Profit & Loss \(P&L\) Statement: The True Measure of Performance Also known as the Income Statement, this shows your profitability over a period \(e.g., a month or a year\). It matches your revenues against the expenses incurred to generate them, following the accrual principle \(recording revenue when it's earned and expenses when they're incurred, not necessarily when cash changes hands\). It answers the question: "Is my business actually making money?")
