2411 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Case Study: "Tunde's Tech Supplies": The Power of Analysis Tunde sold laptops. He noticed his revenue was growing, but his net profit was stagnant. By analyzing his P&L, he saw that his Gross Profit Margin had fallen from 25% to 18%. Digging deeper into his COGS, he realized the cost of one specific laptop model had increased, but he hadn't adjusted its selling price. He also noticed his "transport" expense had doubled. Further investigation revealed his delivery rider was taking inefficient routes. By raising the price of that one model and optimizing delivery routes, Tunde restored his margins and increased his net profit. This is the power of financial analysis.)
/E (Case Study: "Tunde's Tech Supplies": The Power of Analysis Tunde sold laptops. He noticed his revenue was growing, but his net profit was stagnant. By analyzing his P&L, he saw that his Gross Profit Margin had fallen from 25% to 18%. Digging deeper into his COGS, he realized the cost of one specific laptop model had increased, but he hadn't adjusted its selling price. He also noticed his "transport" expense had doubled. Further investigation revealed his delivery rider was taking inefficient routes. By raising the price of that one model and optimizing delivery routes, Tunde restored his margins and increased his net profit. This is the power of financial analysis.)
/Pg 109 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
