/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (This chapter is a deep, practical guide to navigating this complex terrain. We will dismantle the dangerous myths of pricing most notably, the "Cost-Plus" fallacy and introduce you to a multi-dimensional framework for setting prices that not only cover your costs but also capture the true value you create for your customers. We will explore the unique psychology of the Naija customer, who demands both quality and value, and often sees price as the primary indicator of both. You will learn how to structure your prices, communicate their value, and defend them against the inevitable "Your price is too high" negotiation. This is about moving from guessing to strategic pricing, from leaving money on the table to building a profitable, sustainable enterprise.)
/E (This chapter is a deep, practical guide to navigating this complex terrain. We will dismantle the dangerous myths of pricing most notably, the "Cost-Plus" fallacy and introduce you to a multi-dimensional framework for setting prices that not only cover your costs but also capture the true value you create for your customers. We will explore the unique psychology of the Naija customer, who demands both quality and value, and often sees price as the primary indicator of both. You will learn how to structure your prices, communicate their value, and defend them against the inevitable "Your price is too high" negotiation. This is about moving from guessing to strategic pricing, from leaving money on the table to building a profitable, sustainable enterprise.)
/Pg 112 0 R
/K [2]
>>
