2460 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (You Under-price: If your costs are low and your value is high, you leave massive amounts of profit on the table. You train your customers to expect unsustainable low prices and attract the most price-sensitive \(and often least loyal\) segment of the market. You Overprice: If your costs are high due to inefficiency, you simply pass that inefficiency on to the customer, making your product uncompetitive. The market does not care about your high costs; it only cares about the value it receives.)
/E (You Under-price: If your costs are low and your value is high, you leave massive amounts of profit on the table. You train your customers to expect unsustainable low prices and attract the most price-sensitive \(and often least loyal\) segment of the market. You Overprice: If your costs are high due to inefficiency, you simply pass that inefficiency on to the customer, making your product uncompetitive. The market does not care about your high costs; it only cares about the value it receives.)
/Pg 113 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
