/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (In the vibrant, chaotic, and deeply relational marketplace of Nigeria, a transaction is never just an exchange of goods for money. It is a social contract, a test of trust, and the beginning of a relationship. The global, transactional model of sales "here is the product, here is the price, take it or leave it" fails spectacularly here. The Nigerian customer does not just buy a product; they buy the person selling it, the story behind it, and the feeling of being valued. To master the art of the sell in Nigeria is to master the art of human connection. It is about understanding the unspoken rules of engagement, the deep-seated psychological drivers, and the cultural nuances that turn a one-time buyer into a lifelong advocate.)
/E (In the vibrant, chaotic, and deeply relational marketplace of Nigeria, a transaction is never just an exchange of goods for money. It is a social contract, a test of trust, and the beginning of a relationship. The global, transactional model of sales "here is the product, here is the price, take it or leave it" fails spectacularly here. The Nigerian customer does not just buy a product; they buy the person selling it, the story behind it, and the feeling of being valued. To master the art of the sell in Nigeria is to master the art of human connection. It is about understanding the unspoken rules of engagement, the deep-seated psychological drivers, and the cultural nuances that turn a one-time buyer into a lifelong advocate.)
/Pg 143 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
2870 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (This chapter is a deep dive into the heart of Naija commerce. We will move beyond sales scripts and techniques to explore the cultural and psychological landscape of the Nigerian consumer. You will learn how to build trust in an environment of skepticism, how to communicate value in a price-sensitive market, and how to manage customer relationships in a way that fosters legendary loyalty. This is not about manipulation; it is about authentic persuasion. It is about becoming a student of your customer, understanding their fears and aspirations, and positioning your product as the bridge between their current reality and their desired future.)
/E (This chapter is a deep dive into the heart of Naija commerce. We will move beyond sales scripts and techniques to explore the cultural and psychological landscape of the Nigerian consumer. You will learn how to build trust in an environment of skepticism, how to communicate value in a price-sensitive market, and how to manage customer relationships in a way that fosters legendary loyalty. This is not about manipulation; it is about authentic persuasion. It is about becoming a student of your customer, understanding their fears and aspirations, and positioning your product as the bridge between their current reality and their desired future.)
/Pg 143 0 R
/K [5]
>>
