/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (In the grand narrative of a Naija business, the climax is not the sale. The climax is the moment the product successfully lands in the customer's hands, intact and on time. This final leg of the journey the distribution and delivery is where many brilliant businesses and beautiful products meet their untimely end. It is a stage fraught with peril: the "go-slow" that turns a 30-minute trip into a 3-hour ordeal, the dispatch rider who vanishes with your goods, the courier company whose "next-day delivery" promise is a hopeful fiction, the customer whose address is "the big white house after the church, before the generator repair shop.")
/E (In the grand narrative of a Naija business, the climax is not the sale. The climax is the moment the product successfully lands in the customer's hands, intact and on time. This final leg of the journey the distribution and delivery is where many brilliant businesses and beautiful products meet their untimely end. It is a stage fraught with peril: the "go-slow" that turns a 30-minute trip into a 3-hour ordeal, the dispatch rider who vanishes with your goods, the courier company whose "next-day delivery" promise is a hopeful fiction, the customer whose address is "the big white house after the church, before the generator repair shop.")
