/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (The successful scaling described in the previous chapter is a mechanical impossibility without a fundamental human transformation. You cannot personally oversee multiple locations, manage proliferating product lines, or ensure franchise consistency by yourself. The business has outgrown the founder. This juncture marks the most profound and challenging transition in an entrepreneur's journey: the shift from being a solitary operator to being a leader of people. Your role is no longer to do the work, but to build a system where others can do the work excellently, consistently, and with shared purpose. This system is your company culture.)
/E (The successful scaling described in the previous chapter is a mechanical impossibility without a fundamental human transformation. You cannot personally oversee multiple locations, manage proliferating product lines, or ensure franchise consistency by yourself. The business has outgrown the founder. This juncture marks the most profound and challenging transition in an entrepreneur's journey: the shift from being a solitary operator to being a leader of people. Your role is no longer to do the work, but to build a system where others can do the work excellently, consistently, and with shared purpose. This system is your company culture.)
/Pg 183 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
3417 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (In the Naija context, where informal "family" structures often clash with the need for professional standards, building a strong culture is both uniquely difficult and critically important. A powerful culture is your secret weapon. It is what allows you to scale without losing your soul, to maintain quality across distances, and to attract and retain the talented people who will become the future leaders of your enterprise. This chapter is a deep dive into the art and science of moving from a one-man squad to a high-performing, cohesive team.)
/E (In the Naija context, where informal "family" structures often clash with the need for professional standards, building a strong culture is both uniquely difficult and critically important. A powerful culture is your secret weapon. It is what allows you to scale without losing your soul, to maintain quality across distances, and to attract and retain the talented people who will become the future leaders of your enterprise. This chapter is a deep dive into the art and science of moving from a one-man squad to a high-performing, cohesive team.)
/Pg 183 0 R
/K [5]
