3665 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The previous chapter was an inward journey, focusing on the resilience required to sustain yourself on the entrepreneurial path. This final chapter turns that focus outward, exploring the ultimate purpose and impact of your journey. What is it all for? When the daily grind of cash flow, customer complaints, and staff management subsides, what remains? For the truly successful Naija entrepreneur, the answer transcends personal wealth. It is about Legacy building something that outlives you and positively impacts your community. It is about understanding that with the privilege of success comes a profound responsibility to give back.)
/E (The previous chapter was an inward journey, focusing on the resilience required to sustain yourself on the entrepreneurial path. This final chapter turns that focus outward, exploring the ultimate purpose and impact of your journey. What is it all for? When the daily grind of cash flow, customer complaints, and staff management subsides, what remains? For the truly successful Naija entrepreneur, the answer transcends personal wealth. It is about Legacy building something that outlives you and positively impacts your community. It is about understanding that with the privilege of success comes a profound responsibility to give back.)
/Pg 202 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
3666 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (In the Nigerian context, the concept of "giving back" is often narrowly defined as philanthropic donations, often under societal pressure. This chapter reframes it as Strategic Social Responsibility a holistic approach where your business itself becomes a force for good, creating a virtuous cycle that strengthens both your enterprise and your community. This is the final evolution of the Naija entrepreneur: from Hustler, to CEO, to Leader, and finally, to Elder a respected custodian of wealth, wisdom, and opportunity for the next generation.)
/E (In the Nigerian context, the concept of "giving back" is often narrowly defined as philanthropic donations, often under societal pressure. This chapter reframes it as Strategic Social Responsibility a holistic approach where your business itself becomes a force for good, creating a virtuous cycle that strengthens both your enterprise and your community. This is the final evolution of the Naija entrepreneur: from Hustler, to CEO, to Leader, and finally, to Elder a respected custodian of wealth, wisdom, and opportunity for the next generation.)
/Pg 202 0 R
